WEBVTT

c1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Welcome to Operations and Facilities. This session covers facility management, procurement, and supply chain fundamentals.

c2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:20.000
Facility management is responsible for buildings, grounds, utilities, and asset maintenance. Assets under care include computers, printers, servers, filing cabinets, cash safes, and office equipment.

c3
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:32.000
Procurement follows a defined approval flow: request, budget check, vendor selection, purchase order, delivery verification, and payment. Contracts above a threshold require board approval.

c4
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:44.000
The supply chain function manages inventory, vendor relationships, and just-in-time replenishment for perishables like kitchen ingredients and consumables.

c5
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:56.000
Every asset should be under the care of a specific function or sub-function head. Asset registers are reconciled quarterly.

c6
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:08.000
Vendor onboarding requires GST registration verification, bank details, and a signed contract. Vendors performing recurring services need periodic performance reviews.

c7
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:20.000
Supply chain risks include stock-outs during festival demand, vendor concentration, and quality failures. Contingency vendors are maintained for critical categories.

c8
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:32.000
Facility management coordinates with health, safety, and security for compliance walkthroughs and periodic hazard reviews.
